{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["Also regarding Rosh HaShanah it is written ועשיתם עולה. What is different from all the others, for which והקרבתם is written? And if you ask: because it is the Day of Judgment, and once they enter into judgment they are made a new creation — and this is what the liturgical poet composed: 'who create a new creation.' And it must be said after the אוחז, for it deals with judgment. But according to the midrash it appears that it should not be recited except on Yom HaKippurim, for it is written in the book of Tehillim: ועם נברא יהלל יה, and it concludes: about whom was this verse said? Rav and Rabbi Yochanan — one said: about the generation of Mordecai and Esther; and one said: it was said about every generation, for they die every year through their evil deeds, and the Holy One, blessed be He, gives them life on Yom HaKippurim, when He forgives them their sins and creates them as a new creation — and this is: ועם נברא יהלל יה."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:20.117392878Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}